{"notes": "Sector breadth has stepped down from a perfect 1.00 to 0.91 and held there flat for six readings — this is a discrete regime shift in participation, not noise, and it has persisted long enough to be real. Cyclical-minus-defensive is consistently negative/flat, corroborating a mild rotation away from risk-on leadership, and dispersion is compressing back toward the low end of its range — classic narrowing-breadth-under-calm-vol signature. Vol regime itself shows no stress: VIX oscillates 15-20 with no trend, vol risk premium sits in a normal 0.04-0.13 band with the latest print mid-range. This is the classic disagreement case flagged: participation narrowing while the price of volatility stays sanguine. I trust breadth's own-panel read over vol here for the medium-term composition of the rally, but vol_regime's own measurement is genuinely flat/calm, so I report it as such rather than importing breadth's warning into it.

Positioning (asset manager z-score) has round-tripped from ~1.9 z (crowded long) down to ~1.1 z with four straight weeks of unwind (change_4w negative for five months running) — deleveraging, not panic. Leveraged funds show no consistent directional trend, oscillating near zero. Risk appetite proxies (copper/gold, curve, dollar) are flat with no directional trend — no strong risk-on or risk-off impulse there.

